cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pnadc-https: local, standardized repositories of IBGE PNAD Contínua microdata"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maciente
    given-names: Aguinaldo
    alias: amaciente
repository-code: "https://github.com/amaciente/pnadc-https"
abstract: >-
  Command-line tool and Python API that maintains a local repository of
  Brazilian IBGE PNAD Contínua (Continuous National Household Sample Survey)
  microdata. It mirrors the official quarterly and annual Microdados trees
  over HTTPS, parses the IBGE fixed-width dictionaries into stable JSON
  layouts, and converts microdata to Parquet or CSV for analysis in Python
  or R.
keywords:
  - PNAD Contínua
  - IBGE
  - microdata
  - Brazil
  - household survey
  - Parquet
  - reproducible research
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.3.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: "pynad: An application to manage Pnadc microdata and its panels"
    authors:
      - family-names: Osorio
        given-names: Rafael Guerreiro
        affiliation: Instituto de Pesquisa Econômica Aplicada (Ipea)
    version: 3.0.3
    license: GPL-3.0-or-later
    url: "https://pypi.org/project/pynad/"
    notes: >-
      pnadc is derived from pynad, which originated the workflow it
      implements.
  - type: software
    title: "PNADcIBGE: Downloading, Reading and Analyzing PNADC Microdata"
    authors:
      - family-names: Assuncao
        given-names: Gabriel
      - family-names: Braga
        given-names: Douglas
    license: GPL-3.0
    url: "https://cran.r-project.org/package=PNADcIBGE"
    notes: >-
      IBGE's official R package; informed the column-selection workflow and
      the documentation of deflators and survey design.
